            "review_title": "Review at Crazy Bee Cafe",
            "review_text": "mybraintravels\nHamburg, Germany51 contributions\n0\nVery nice atmospheric Cafe!\nMar 2016 • Couples\nWe found this little sweet café by accident and went in spontaneous. What a good decision! :-) The Vietnamese Coffee where excellent (hot and cold) and you get free, homemade, delicious, tea (on ice) - as much as you like.\nBut the greatest thing was the nice atmosphere. The furnitures where from wood and also the ceiling where wooden with little lights in it. One wall (wooden, as well ;-D) was decorated with empty wine bottles, used as flower pots. Flower pots where also everywhere else in the outside area. The café was very clean inside and seemed to be comfortable and cute as well.\nThe Service was very nice and the price (15000 VND for a coffee) very affordable!\nThe Cafe opened only 1 month ago. So, we really recommend a visit to help it to exist many more years! :-)\nEnjoy!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 23, 2016",
